    "evidence_text": "hnRNP A1 associates with telomere ends and stimulates telomerase activity.\n\nG-quadruplex structure in a DNA substrate can block its extension by telomerase.\n\nThe yeast Pif1p helicase removes telomerase from telomeric DNA\n\nTelomeres are the physical ends of eukaryotic chromosomes.\n\nPif1 family helicases suppress genome instability at G-quadruplex motifs\n\nHowever, the structural basis for specific G-quadruplex recognition by proteins has not been understood.\n\nOur structure explains how RHAU specifically recognizes parallel G-quadruplexes.\n\nIn general, G4 motifs were underrepresented in genes.\n\nWe have previously shown that HR facilitates telomere replication.\n\nFailure of untangling them in the cell impedes DNA-based transactions and leads to genome instability.\n\nCells have evolved highly specific helicases to resolve G4 structures.\n\nThis finding provides new insights into the properties and functions of G4s.\n\nTelomestatin is able to stabilize G-quadruplex structures that are formed from duplex human telomeric DNA as well as from single-stranded DNA.\n\nRational design of acridine-based ligands with selectivity for human telomeric quadruplexes.",
